<h1>Documentation</h1>
<p class="lead">toke reference documentation — language spec, standard library, and tutorials.</p>

<h2>Getting Started</h2>
<p>New to toke? Start here.</p>
<ul>
  <li><a href="/docs/learn/hello-world">Hello World</a> — write, compile, and run your first toke program</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/learn/install">Install</a> — build toke from source on macOS or Linux</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/learn/tour">Language Tour</a> — a fast overview of toke syntax and features</li>
</ul>

<h2>Learn</h2>
<p>Step-by-step tutorials covering the full language.</p>
<ul>
  <li><a href="/docs/learn/01-why-toke">Why toke?</a> — motivation, design goals, and Gate 1 results</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/learn/02-modules-functions">Modules &amp; Functions</a> — the building blocks of every toke program</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/learn/03-control-flow">Control Flow</a> — if, loop, and early return</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/learn/04-collections">Collections</a> — arrays and maps with @() syntax</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/learn/05-errors">Errors</a> — structured error types and recovery</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/learn/06-strings-io">Strings &amp; I/O</a> — working with text and the file system</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/learn/07-modules-imports">Modules &amp; Imports</a> — organising larger programs</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/learn/08-advanced">Advanced</a> — FFI, pointers, casts and arena blocks</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/learn/09-stdlib">Standard Library</a> — a deep dive into the stdlib modules</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/learn/10-project">Project</a> — build a complete application</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/learn/11-patterns-and-efficiency">Patterns &amp; Efficiency</a> — the measured pattern catalogue</li>
</ul>

<h2>Reference</h2>
<p>Precise specifications for the language and standard library.</p>
<ul>
  <li><a href="/docs/reference/grammar">Grammar</a> — the complete backtrack-free grammar in BNF</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/reference/types">Types</a> — the type system: primitives, structs, and enums</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/reference/errors">Error Codes</a> — machine-readable compiler error reference</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/reference/package-manifest">Packages</a> — the <code>pkg.toml</code> manifest, the pinned <code>pkg.lock</code>, and the <code>tkc pkg</code> commands</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/compiler/python-view">Python View</a> — <code>tkc --python-view</code>, a read-only Python-like rendering of toke source for review</li>
</ul>

<h2>Architecture &amp; Security</h2>
<ul>
  <li><a href="/docs/architecture/binary-ir-design">Binary IR (.tkir)</a> — the <code>.tkir</code> 1.2 format and <code>tkc --emit-tkir</code>, <code>--from-tkir</code> and <code>--read-tkir</code></li>
  <li><a href="/docs/security/threat-model">Threat Model</a> — the corpus pipeline, the compiler, runtime and web trust boundaries, and toke's post-quantum posture</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/security/pqc-hndl-triage">PQC: Key-Exchange Triage</a> — every harvest-now-decrypt-later exposure in the tree and its status</li>
  <li><a href="/docs/security/pqc-signatures-roadmap">PQC: Signatures Roadmap</a> — the migration plan from Ed25519 and ECDSA to ML-DSA</li>
</ul>

